BEGIN NOTES;
[Taxon comments]
TEXT TAXON=48 TEXT='I have serious doubts that the bone identified by Dzik and Sulej 2016 as a jugal is a jugal, instead the bone identified as a quadratojugal looks more like a jugal. Thus, both jugal and quadratojugal are scored with question marks (MDE, 18 June 2023).';
TEXT TAXON=99 TEXT='Scorings of added characters based on UMZC and BPI specimens (MDE, 12 September 2012).';
TEXT TAXON=101 TEXT='The scorings were based on the description of Tatarinov (1978), descrption and figures of Benton and Allen (1997) and personal observations on the specimen. The figures of Tatarinov (1978) were not considered because of discrepancies with the photographs of Benton and Allen (1997) and strange morphology when compared with other basal archosauromorphs (MDE, 2 April 2015).';
TEXT TAXON=105 TEXT='The referred cervical vertebrae are interpreted as Cv3-5 (MDE, 7 February 2022)';
TEXT TAXON=109 TEXT='PIN 1025/348 (MDE, 7 February 2022)';
TEXT TAXON=114 TEXT='QMF9532 is interpreted as Cv3-5, QMF60371 as Cv6, QMF9533 as Cv8 (MDE, 07 February 2022)';
TEXT TAXON=116 TEXT='It includes the archosauriform vertebrae from the Arcadia Formation, the holotypic maxilla and the referred pterygoid (MDE, 06 August 2022)';
TEXT TAXON=124 TEXT='The holotype is interpreted as a Cv9 (MDE, 7 February 2022)';
TEXT TAXON=125 TEXT='It includes the holotype of the species (Cv9) and its referred specimens PIN 1025/14 (parabasisphenoid), PIN 1025/15 (postorbital), PIN 1025/355 (very anterior dorsal vertebra), PIN 1025/404 (scapula), PIN1025/405 (coracoid), PIN 1025/406 (ilium), and PIN 1025/419 (probable D1), and the holotype of Blomosuchus (parabasisphenoid) and its referred specimens PIN 1025/420 (Cv3-5) and PIN 1025/425 (femur) (MDE, 7 February 2022)';
TEXT TAXON=126 TEXT='The holotypes are interpreted as Cv3-5 (MDE, 7 February 2022)';
TEXT TAXON=127 TEXT='The vertebrae of the holotype are interpreted as Cv8 and Cv9 (MDE, 7 February 2022)';
TEXT TAXON=128 TEXT='Include holotype PIN 2252 381 and referred specimens PIN 3200 212, 3200 217, 3200 472, 2243 167, 2252 384, 2252 386, 2424 6 (holotype of Tsylmosuchus samariensis), and 4332 1 (holotype of Tsylmosuchus jakovlevi) (MDE, 14 September 2020).';
TEXT TAXON=129 TEXT='The holotype PIN 3361/13 is interpreted as Cv3-5 and referred specimen PIN 3361/14 as a Cv8 (MDE, 7 January 2022)';
TEXT TAXON=130 TEXT='The holotype is interpreted as a probable Cv5 (MDE, 7 January 2022)';
TEXT TAXON=139 TEXT='The anteriormost preserved vertebra of the holotype is interpreted as a Cv8 (MDE, 7 February 2022)';
TEXT TAXON=152 TEXT='The tentatively referred specimens of Sookias et al. (2014) (partial pterygoid and lower jaw) were not included here because there is no possitive evidence for this referral. Sookias et al. (2014) stated that "These referrals are, however, plausible because no other archosauromorphs have been found at the locality", but this argument is circular (MDE, 18 August 2014).';
TEXT TAXON=154 TEXT='The tentatively referred specimens of Sookias et al. (2014) (partial pterygoid and lower jaw) were not included here because there is no possitive evidence for this referral. Sookias et al. (2014) stated that "These referrals are, however, plausible because no other archosauromorphs have been found at the locality", but this argument is circular (MDE, 18 August 2014).';
TEXT TAXON=159 TEXT='The specimens that were not associated with the holotype and do not possess overlapping features with bones collected in the type excavation site are not included in the scorings. These non-associated bones usually are of bigger animals and sometimes possess non-congruent characters with those expected for the animal of the type excavation site. The very poorly preserved maxilla and supposed attached premaxilla were not included because they seem to belong to a bigger animal than the holotype. It was not included here the premaxilla-maxilla (ISI R334/1), right jugal (reinterpreted as an indeterminate bone, ISI R334/3), left quadrate-quadratojugal (reinterpreted as an indeterminate bone, ISI R334/4), right squamosal (reinterpreted as a right postorbital, ISI R334/5), right pterygoid (the indentification of this bone as a pterygoid is very tentative, ISI R334/7), and left pterygoid (ISI R334/6) (MDE, 16 March 2015).';
TEXT TAXON=163 TEXT='Including new scores from first hand scoring of PVSJ 606';
TEXT TAXON=167 TEXT='Scorings with holotype in hand';
TEXT TAXON=188 TEXT='Nicrosaurus kapffi: NHMUK R38036, 38037, 42743, 42744, 42745, multiple SMNS specimens (SMNS specimens with ambiguous identification were not considered), Huene 1923, Hungerbühler 1998, 2000 (MDE, 19 August 2014).';
TEXT TAXON=189 TEXT='UCMP 26699, UCMP 27200, MCZ 1029, USNM 18313 and Camp (1930) (MDE, 6 May 2014).';
TEXT TAXON=190 TEXT='Huene 1914, Walker 1964, Sereno 1991 (MDE, 20 August 2014).';
TEXT TAXON=234 TEXT='The postfrontal was not originally scored by Nesbitt et al. 2023 and this decision is followed here (MDE, 27 July 2023)';
TEXT TAXON=267 TEXT='The vertebrae have not been included in the socrings following Langer and Ferigolo (2013): They fit the general morphology of archosaur vertebrae, but most lack unambiguous dinosauromorph apomorphies. Indeed, their referral to S. agudoensis must be treated with caution, especially for the purpose of character coding in phylogenetic analyses. (MDE, October 28, 2020)';
TEXT TAXON=285 TEXT='This terminal includes also the hypodigm of Plateosaurus erlenbergiensis (MDE, 01 November 2020).';
