TEXT CHARACTER=435 TEXT='Rationale_for_new_limits_explained_in_spreadsheet_(ML).';
TEXT CHARACTER=510 TEXT='I_changed_this_character._Petrolacosaurus_clearly_has_a_chunky_broad_femur,_as_does_Youngina._4/1_is_the_new_ratio,_not_3/1_(RR)._Problem:_then_Youngina_has_1_and_Hyperodapedon_and_Apsisaurus_0._State_1_redefined_slightly_(ML).';
[Attribute comments]
TEXT CHARACTER=1 TAXON=111 TEXT='The absence of interdental plates is particularly evident in the anterior end of the right dentary (UTGD 54655) (MDE, 12 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=1 TAXON=151 TEXT='Based on UMZC T6921 (MDE, 28 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=1 TAXON=188 TEXT='Nicrosaurus kapffi: NHMUK R38036, 38037, 42743, 42744, 42745, Huene 1923, Hungerbühler 1998, 2000; Nicrosaurus sp. Hungerbühler, 1998 (MDE';
TEXT CHARACTER=2 TAXON=236 TEXT='ratio=0.56-0.58 (MDE, 20-2-2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=5 TAXON=199 TEXT='The dorsal surface of the skull of available specimens is too damaged to determine the state of this character (MDE, 7 May 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=8 TAXON=24 TEXT='The parietals have a median, longitudinal sagital crest, and the surface immediately lateral to it are not depressed as it should be the case in a supratemporal fossa (NMK S 180) (MDE, 13 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=8 TAXON=88 TEXT='Based on Whatley (2005: 19).';
TEXT CHARACTER=9 TAXON=73 TEXT='Dilkes (1998: character 10) scored Mesosuchus has having confluent external nares and the condition is clearly visible in SAM-PK-6536 (MDE, 27 August 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=14 TAXON=164 TEXT='In the holotype the anterior border of the antorbital fenestra is pointed, whereas in PVL 4606 is gently rounded (MDE, 7 July 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=15 TAXON=266 TEXT='The secondary antorbital fenestra occurs is defined by the premaxilla, maxilla and sometimes nasal. In Heterodontosaurus the accesory antorbital fenestra is completely enclosed by the maxilla within the antorbital fossa and, as a result, is not considered homologous to the former (MDE, 27 August, 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=16 TAXON=170 TEXT='The skull is strongly dorsoventrally compressed beause of taphonomic processes and the character cannot be confidently scored (MDE, 18 August 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=19 TAXON=24 TEXT='Based on Gottman-Quesada and Sander (2009: fig. 9) (MDE, 12 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=19 TAXON=73 TEXT='See discussion of Modesto and Sues (2004: 347) regarding the scoring of this character in Mesosuchus (MDE, 16 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=19 TAXON=101 TEXT='Based on Tatarinov (1978: 508) (MDE, 25 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=19 TAXON=104 TEXT='In SAM-PK-K10603 the posttemporal fenestra cannot be observed, but it may be a result of the strong dorsoventral artificial compression suffered by the skull. In RC 846 the posttemporal fenestra is present as a foramen (MDE, 5 September 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=19 TAXON=160 TEXT='Based on Dilkes and Arcucci (2012: 17) (MDE, 13 April 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=20 TAXON=7 TEXT='The ratio based on the preserved mould of rostrum is 0.38 and it could have been slightly higher if the rostrum extended more anteriorly, thus, it was scored as 0/1 (MDE, 25 May 2021).';
TEXT CHARACTER=20 TAXON=279 TEXT='ratio=0.50 (MDE, 22-2-2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=21 TAXON=5 TEXT='The skulls that preserve the anterir tip of the maxilla are strongly dorsoventrally compressed and, as a result, the scoring is codified as missing data (MDE, 7 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=21 TAXON=165 TEXT='ratio=0.27 (PVL 4604) (MDE, 19-2-2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=21 TAXON=248 TEXT='ratio = <0.41 (MDE, 11 November 2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=22 TAXON=16 TEXT='Based on Evans (1980: fig. 1) (MDE, 20 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=22 TAXON=24 TEXT='The condition of this character cannot be confidently assessed because the skulls of Protorosaurus are hevely crushed and compressed (MDE, 3 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=22 TAXON=141 TEXT='Based on BP/1/5207 and NHMUK R5392 (MDE, 21 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=25 TAXON=141 TEXT='Based on the right side of BP/1/5207 (MDE, 21 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=25 TAXON=151 TEXT='SAM-PK-6048 lacks a subnarial foramen, but SAM-PK-6047 possesses a subnarial foramen formed by a notch on the maxilla (MDE, 31 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=25 TAXON=203 TEXT='Based on Butler et al. (2014) (MDE, 22 August 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=27 TAXON=5 TEXT='Based on Gow (1975: fig. 1) (MDE, 15 October 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=28 TAXON=153 TEXT='ratio < 3.14 (Sues et al. 2024: fig. 3a) (MDE, 9 August 2024)';
TEXT CHARACTER=28 TAXON=254 TEXT='ratio >2.27 (MDE, 7 July 2022)';
TEXT CHARACTER=29 TAXON=133 TEXT='The palatal process of the maxilla is distinctly anteroventrally oriented and in other basal archosauriforms the palatal process of the premaxilla forms a ventrally facing obtuse angle with the alveolar margin of the bone. As a result, the premaxilla of Kalisuchus should have been downturned, resembling the condition in proterosuchids and Sarmatosuchus (MDE, 18 September 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=29 TAXON=141 TEXT='Based on the articulated skull BP/1/5207 (MDE, 21 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=29 TAXON=153 TEXT='Based on the orientation of the palatal process of the maxilla (MDE, 09 August 2024)';
TEXT CHARACTER=31 TAXON=236 TEXT='The type of preservation and size of the specimen probably turn very difficult to determine the condition of this character (MDE, 20-2-2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=31 TAXON=238 TEXT='The type of preservation and size of the specimen probably turn very difficult to determine the condition of this character (MDE, 23 August 2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=32 TAXON=35 TEXT='I can''t discern the pineal foramen in BSPG 1995 I 5 and Gottman-Quesada and Sander (2009) didn';
TEXT CHARACTER=32 TAXON=37 TEXT='The suture between the frontals and parietals is not clear in AM 3585 (MDE, 4 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=33 TAXON=143 TEXT='Based on Gower (2003: 15) (MDE, 25 September 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=34 TAXON=5 TEXT='Based on GHG K 106 (MDE, 7 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=35 TAXON=29 TEXT='Based on Peyer (1937: fig. 32) (MDE, 17 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=36 TAXON=5 TEXT='Based on BP/1/2871 (MDE, 27 March 2015).';
TEXT CHARACTER=36 TAXON=60 TEXT='The dorsolateral process of the premaxilla is well extended beyond the posteiror margin of the external naris (Spielmann et al. 2008: fig. 20). Accordingly, the scoring of this character was changed from (?) to (1) (MDE, 4 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=36 TAXON=101 TEXT='Based on Tatarinov (1978: 508) (MDE, 2 April 2015).';
TEXT CHARACTER=37 TAXON=149 TEXT='The posterior margin of the base of the postnarial process is broken off, but the facet for its reception on the maxilla shows that it was plate-like (MDE, 1 October 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=39 TAXON=24 TEXT='Based on Gottman-Quesada and Sander (2009: 140): the maxilla is underlain by the subnarial process of the premaxilla (MDE, 13 May 2021)';
TEXT CHARACTER=42 TAXON=5 TEXT='Based on Broom (1922:273) and Gow (1975) (MDE,12 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=42 TAXON=16 TEXT='Based on Evans (1980: 223) (MDE, 20 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=42 TAXON=24 TEXT='Based on Gottman-Quesada and Sander (2009: 140) (MDE, 3 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=42 TAXON=73 TEXT='Mesosuchus has two premaxillary teeth (Dilkes, 1998: 511) (MDE, 27 August 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=42 TAXON=101 TEXT='Based on Tatarinov (1978: 510) (MDE, 2 April 2015).';
TEXT CHARACTER=42 TAXON=164 TEXT='Based on the left premaxilla of PVL 4601 (MDE, 7 July 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=42 TAXON=165 TEXT='Based on Trotteyn et al. (2013) (MDE, 9 July 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=44 TAXON=135 TEXT='The holotype of Sarmatosuchus seems to be non-fully grown specimen because of the presence of an open neurocentral suture in the dorsal centrum (MDE, 9 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=44 TAXON=170 TEXT='The premaxillary teeth are lateroventrally oriented, but it may be a result of the strong dorsoventral compressio suffered by the skull (PVSJ 567) (MDE, 28 April 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=45 TAXON=5 TEXT='Based on SAM-PK-K7578 (MDE, 6 September 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=45 TAXON=16 TEXT='The presence of a septomaxilla is equivocal (Evans 1980: 220) (MDE, 20 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=45 TAXON=38 TEXT='Following Dilkes (1998) and Nosotti (2007) (MDE, 2 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=45 TAXON=60 TEXT='Based on Gregory (1945: 277) (MDE, 25 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=45 TAXON=73 TEXT='Based on SAM-PK-6536. Inside the narial cavity, there is a pair of plate-like bones, with a dorsally raised medial margin that are almost identical to the septomaxillae of BP/1/4016 (MDE, 27 December 2015).';
TEXT CHARACTER=45 TAXON=99 TEXT='The septomaxilla of Prolacerta broomi possesses a curved lateral lip (Modesto and Sues, 2004) and, as a result, is not a completely flat sheet of bone. Accordingly, the scording of this character was changed from (2) to (1) (MDE, 11 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=49 TAXON=5 TEXT='Based on GHG K 106 (MDE, 7 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=49 TAXON=20 TEXT='Based on Evans (1990: 208) (MDE, 4 April 2015).';
TEXT CHARACTER=50 TAXON=164 TEXT='ratio = 0.67 (MDE, 4 July 2022)';
TEXT CHARACTER=50 TAXON=290 TEXT='ratio = 0.39 (MDE, 07 November 2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=51 TAXON=142 TEXT='Based on Wang et al. (2013: fig 2a) (MDE, 27 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=52 TAXON=1 TEXT='Based on Reisz (1977: fig. 2) (MDE, 18 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=52 TAXON=24 TEXT='Based on Modesto and Sues (2004) and Gottman-Quesada and Sander (2009) (MDE, 16 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=52 TAXON=29 TEXT='Based on PIMUZ T4822 (MDE, 16 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=52 TAXON=151 TEXT='The anterior maxillary foramen is absent in SAM-PK-13665 but it is present in other specimens (Gow 1970) (MDE, 16 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=52 TAXON=236 TEXT='The type of preservation and size of the specimen probably turn very difficult to determine the condition of this character (MDE, 20-2-2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=54 TAXON=189 TEXT='Based on UCMP 27200 and Nesbitt (2011: 96) (MDE, 6 May 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=55 TAXON=178 TEXT='0.24 based on Foffa et al. 2020 (MDE, 13 July 2021)';
TEXT CHARACTER=55 TAXON=290 TEXT='ratio = ca. 0.5 (MDE, 07 November 2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=59 TAXON=29 TEXT='Based on PIMUZ T4355 (MDE, 29 August 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=59 TAXON=204 TEXT='Both character-states are present in MCZ 4117 (MDE, 18 September 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=61 TAXON=38 TEXT='Based on WIld (1973: fig. 5, 6) (MDE, 20 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=63 TAXON=106 TEXT='Most of the suture between maxilla and jugal cannot be diserned possibly because of the partial fusion between both bones (NMQR 880) (MDE, 24 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=63 TAXON=151 TEXT='Based on SAM-PK-6047A and the left side of SAM-PK-5867 (MDE, 18 September 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=63 TAXON=290 TEXT='Horizontal process tapers posteriorly in the holotype and expands dorsally towards the posterior end in PVSJ 561 (MDE, 03 January 2023)';
TEXT CHARACTER=65 TAXON=232 TEXT='The dorsal process is present in UFRGS-PV-0152-T and the dorsal prong of the anterior tip of the jugal figured by Parrish 1993 for UFRGS-PV-0156-T might be a dorsal proess extending from the maxilla (MDE, 4 September 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=66 TAXON=38 TEXT='Based on Wild (1973: fig. 26) (MDE, 7 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=66 TAXON=73 TEXT='Based on Dilkes (1998: 505) and SAM-PK-6536 (MDE, 3 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=66 TAXON=104 TEXT='Based on CT data of BSPG 1934 VIII 514 (MDE, 5 September 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=66 TAXON=151 TEXT='Based on UMZC T692 and Gow (1970) (MDE, 28 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=66 TAXON=152 TEXT='Based on Sookias et al. (2020) (MDE, 12 October 2022).';
TEXT CHARACTER=66 TAXON=190 TEXT='Based on Walker (1964: 72) (MDE, 20 August 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=66 TAXON=204 TEXT='Based on Lecuona (2013) and Butler et al. (2014) (MDE, 22 August 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=67 TAXON=151 TEXT='Based on SAM-PK-6050 (MDE, 21 October 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=68 TAXON=151 TEXT='The ventral margin of the maxilla is slightly convex in SAM-PK-5867 (MDE, 11 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=75 TAXON=16 TEXT='Based on Evans (1980: 225) (MDE, 20 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=75 TAXON=24 TEXT='Gottman-Quesada and Sander (2009: 141) described 28 (+-1) tooth positions in the maxilla of NMK S 180 (MDE, 3 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=75 TAXON=102 TEXT='16 tooth positions based on Pinheiro et al. (2016: 22) (MDE, 05 December 2020)';
TEXT CHARACTER=75 TAXON=193 TEXT='ca. 19-20 tooth positions based on the suture between premaxilla and maxilla on the palate (MDE, 2 October 2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=75 TAXON=207 TEXT='Based on the presence of ca. 11 maxillary teeth and 13 dentary teeth (MDE, 6 July 2022)';
TEXT CHARACTER=75 TAXON=280 TEXT='21-22 tooth positions in the dentary (MDE, 15-3-2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=76 TAXON=5 TEXT='Based on GHG K106 (MDE, 20 November 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=76 TAXON=16 TEXT='Based on Evans (1980: fig. 1c) (MDE, 20 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=76 TAXON=38 TEXT='Based on Wild (1973) (MDE, 2 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=76 TAXON=60 TEXT='No skull of Trilophosaurus buettneri preserves both antorbital and postorbital regions (MDE, 4 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=76 TAXON=164 TEXT='The suture between the frontals and parietals cannot be confidently traced in available specimens (MDE, 8 July 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=76 TAXON=165 TEXT='ratio=1.12 (PVL 4604) (MDE, 19-2-2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=76 TAXON=279 TEXT='ratio=1.10 (MDE, 22-2-2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=77 TAXON=9 TEXT='The snout of AM 3585 is broad and the natural moulds of the nasals indicate that these bones were dorsal elements (MDE, 3 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=77 TAXON=60 TEXT='The snout of Trilophosaurus buettneri is narrow and tall, and the nasal has a strong vertical contribution to the snout (Spielmann et al. 2008: figs. 20-22) (MDE, 4 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=78 TAXON=38 TEXT='Based on PIMUZ T2484 (MDE, 11 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=83 TAXON=141 TEXT='Based on the left side of BP/1/5207 (MDE, 21 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=85 TAXON=38 TEXT='Based on Wild (1973: fig. 1: f.n.) (MDE, 20 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=87 TAXON=164 TEXT='Based on PVL 4606 (MDE, 8 July 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=87 TAXON=190 TEXT='Based on Walker (1964: fig. 3a) (MDE, 20 August 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=89 TAXON=5 TEXT='The foramen for the opening of the nasolacrimal duct could not be located in any of the studies specimens (e.g. BP/1/2459, 3859, GHG K 106, GHG RS 160, TM 1490, 4095) (MDE, 11 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=89 TAXON=53 TEXT='No foramen for the lacrimal duct is present (Flynn et al., 2010: 677) (MDE, 18 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=89 TAXON=60 TEXT='The new interpretations of the skull of Trilophosaurus buettneri strongly differs from those of Gregory (1945) regarding the shape and position of the lacrimal and the foramen showed by this author should not be positioned within the lacrimal based on Parks (1969) and Spielmann et al. (2008). However, the latter author did not give information about the passage of the lacrimal duct in Trilophosaurus buettneri (MDE, 14 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=89 TAXON=104 TEXT='Based on RC 846 (MDE, 5 September 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=89 TAXON=151 TEXT='Based on Senter (2003) (MDE, 28 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=89 TAXON=227 TEXT='Based on Gower (1999: 39) (MDE, 22 April 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=90 TAXON=3 TEXT='The lacrial duct opens laterally on the lacrimal, close to the posterior margin of the bone (MNHN 1908-32-57) (MDE, 10 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=90 TAXON=5 TEXT='The foramen for the opening of the nasolacrimal duct could not be located in any of the studies specimens (e.g. BP/1/2459, 3859, GHG K 106, GHG RS 160, TM 1490, 4095) (MDE, 11 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=90 TAXON=16 TEXT='Based on Evans (1980: 212) (MDE, 20 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=90 TAXON=38 TEXT='Based on Wild (1973: fig. 1: f.n.) (MDE, 20 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=90 TAXON=53 TEXT='No foramen for the lacrimal duct is present (Flynn et al., 2010: 677) (MDE, 18 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=90 TAXON=60 TEXT='The new interpretations of the skull of Trilophosaurus buettneri strongly differs from those of Gregory (1945) regarding the shape and position of the lacrimal and the foramen showed by this author should not be positioned within the lacrimal based on Parks (1969) and Spielmann et al. (2008). However, the latter author did not give information about the passage of the lacrimal duct in Trilophosaurus buettneri (MDE, 14 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=90 TAXON=73 TEXT='Based on Dilkes (1998: 505) (MDE, 13 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=90 TAXON=104 TEXT='Based on RC 846 (MDE, 5 September 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=91 TAXON=5 TEXT='The ventral margin of the ventral temporal bar (i.e. formed by the posterior process of the jugal and the anterior process of the quadratojugal) is concave in BP/1/3859 (MDE, 11 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=91 TAXON=60 TEXT='The ventral margin of the postorbital region of the skull is severely damaged in TMM 31025-140 and the condition of the character cannot be confidently assessed (Spielmann et al. 2008: fig. 19) (MDE, 4 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=92 TAXON=49 TEXT='Based on ZAR 08 (MDE, 1 May 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=95 TAXON=5 TEXT='Based on BP/1/3859 (MDE, 7 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=95 TAXON=29 TEXT='Based on PIMUZ T4822 (MDE, 10 October 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=95 TAXON=49 TEXT='Based on ZAR 08 (MDE, 1 May 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=96 TAXON=164 TEXT='Based on PVL 4606 (MDE, 8 July 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=96 TAXON=190 TEXT='Based on UCMP 27200, MCZ 1029 and Camp (1930: fig. 11) (MDE, 6 May 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=96 TAXON=273 TEXT='Based on Porro et al. (2015: page 17) (MDE, 1-3-2019)';
TEXT CHARACTER=100 TAXON=53 TEXT='The height of the base of the posterior process is measured orthogonally to the main axis of the process (MDE, 18 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=100 TAXON=254 TEXT='ratio = 1.66 (MDE, 7 July 2022)';
TEXT CHARACTER=103 TAXON=99 TEXT='State 0 in SAM-PK-K10797 and state 1 in BP/1/3575 and BP/1/5375 (MDE, 5 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=104 TAXON=141 TEXT='In BP/1/5207 the base of the posterior process of the jugal seems to be semi-elliptical, but it is not the case in BP/1/3893 (MDE, 10 April 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=108 TAXON=3 TEXT='The morphology of the suture between the prefrontal and nasal cannot be confidently determined and, particularly, because the skull is exposed in medial view (MNHN 1908-32-57) (MDE, 11 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=108 TAXON=5 TEXT='The suture between the prefrontal and nasal is anterolaterally oriented along its entire extension (BP/1/3859, GHG K 106) (MDE, 11 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=108 TAXON=38 TEXT='Based on Nosotti (2007: fig. 44) (MDE, 2 Septermber 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=112 TAXON=2 TEXT='The frontals are only preserved in the juvenile specimen (MDE, 11 May 2021)';
TEXT CHARACTER=113 TAXON=29 TEXT='Based on PIMUZ T4822 (MDE, 10 October 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=114 TAXON=60 TEXT='The orbital border of the frontal is broad in TMM 31025-207 (Spielmann et al. 2008: fig. 20e, f). Accordingly, the scoring of this character was changed from (0) to (1) (MDE, 4 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=114 TAXON=141 TEXT='The orbital margin of the frontal is narrow (MDE, 22 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=115 TAXON=38 TEXT='Based on PIMUZ T2189 (MDE, 7 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=116 TAXON=15 TEXT='The posterolateral process of the frontal is long and the suture with the parietal forms an acute angle with the parasagittal plane (Fraser, 1982: fig. 1c). Accordingly, the scoring of this character was changed from (1) to (2) (MDE, 11 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=116 TAXON=38 TEXT='Based on PIMUZ T2189 (MDE, 7 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=116 TAXON=101 TEXT='Based on Tatarinov (1978: 508) (MDE, 2 April 2015).';
TEXT CHARACTER=116 TAXON=104 TEXT='In large specimens of Proterosuchus fergusi (e.g. SAM-PK-K10603) the fr-p suture forms a right to obtuse angle to parasagittal plane, but in smaller specimens (e.g. RC 59) the fr-p suture forms an acute angle, similar to Prolacerta (Modesto & Sues, 2004: fig. 4). Thus, this feature seems to be related to intraspecific variation (probably ontogenetic) in Proterosuchus fergusi (MDE, 19 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=120 TAXON=101 TEXT='Based on Tatarinov (1978: 508) (MDE, 25 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=121 TAXON=29 TEXT='Based on PIMUZ T2472 (MDE, 17 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=123 TAXON=3 TEXT='The anterior end of the anterior process of the preserved postorbital and the parietals are missing. As a result, it is not possible to determine if the postfrontal participated in the supratermporal fenestra or not (i.e. if it was a contact between the postorbital and parietal) (MNHN 1908-32-57) (MDE, 10 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=123 TAXON=38 TEXT='Based on Nosotti (2007: 81) (MDE, 11 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=123 TAXON=53 TEXT='Based on Flynn et al. (2010: 679) (MDE, 14 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=125 TAXON=101 TEXT='The condition is not consistent between Tatarinov (1978) and Benton & Allen (1997) (MDE, 25 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=128 TAXON=3 TEXT='Only the mould of the medial surface of the postorbital is preserved and it cannot be determined the morphology of the lateral surface of the bone (MNHN 1908-32-57). Accordingly, the state of this character was changed from (0) to (?) (MDE, 10 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=130 TAXON=29 TEXT='The posterior process of the quadratojugal does not reach the posterior border of the supratemporal fenesrtra defined by the squamosal (PIMUZ T4822) (MDE, 30 August 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=130 TAXON=104 TEXT='The posterior process of the postorbital extends beyond the posterior margin of the supratemporal fenestra in Proterosuchus fergusi (e.g. BP/1/4016 and SAM-PK-K10603) (MDE, 19 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=131 TAXON=170 TEXT='The skull is strongly dorsoventrally compressed beause of taphonomic processes and the character cannot be confidently scored (MDE, 18 August 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=132 TAXON=208 TEXT='The dorsoventral compression of the skull makes the determination of this feature equivocal (MDE, 27 December 2021)';
TEXT CHARACTER=137 TAXON=53 TEXT='Based on Flynn et al. (2010: fig. 1A) (MDE, 18 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=137 TAXON=99 TEXT='Based on UMZC 2003.41R (MDE, 5 April 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=137 TAXON=101 TEXT='The condition is not consistent between Tatarinov (1978) and Benton & Allen (1997) (MDE, 25 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=138 TAXON=16 TEXT='The condition is almost identical to that of Planocephalosaurus (compare Evans 1980: fig. 1 and Fraser 1982: fig. 1) (MDE, 20 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=139 TAXON=101 TEXT='The condition is not consistent between Tatarinov (1978) and Benton & Allen (1997) (MDE, 25 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=141 TAXON=151 TEXT='Based on the left squamosal of SAM-PK-5867 (MDE, 28 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=145 TAXON=101 TEXT='The condition is not consistent between Tatarinov (1978) and Benton & Allen (1997) (MDE, 25 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=146 TAXON=101 TEXT='The condition is not consistent between Tatarinov (1978) and Benton & Allen (1997) (MDE, 25 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=148 TAXON=101 TEXT='The condition is not consistent between Tatarinov (1978) and Benton & Allen (1997) (MDE, 25 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=150 TAXON=3 TEXT='It is not clear if the quadratojugal was absent or not (Bicklemann et al. 2009) (MDE, 10 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=150 TAXON=16 TEXT='Based on Evans (1980: 216) (MDE, 20 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=150 TAXON=24 TEXT='The presence of a quadratojugal is doubtful in Protorosaurus (MDE, 3 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=150 TAXON=38 TEXT='The quadratojugal is absent (Wild, 1973, Nosotti, 2007) (MDE, 22 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=150 TAXON=60 TEXT='The quadratojugal of TMM 31025-140 is broken and the anterior extent of this bone cannot be assessed with the currently available specimnes (Spielman et al. 2008: fig. 19). As a result, the scoring of this character has been changed from (2) to (?) (MDE, 4 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=150 TAXON=106 TEXT='Based on the facet on the quadrate (NMQR 1484) (MDE, 24 March 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=153 TAXON=24 TEXT='The presence of a quadratojugal is doubtful in Protorosaurus (MDE, 3 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=153 TAXON=29 TEXT='I couldn''t recognize a quadratojugal in Macrocnemus specimens (MDE, 30 August 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=153 TAXON=38 TEXT='Tanystropheus lacks of a quadratojugal (Wild, 1973: figs. 8?10) and Nosotti (2007) (MDE, 20 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=153 TAXON=190 TEXT='Based on the facet along the entire ventral margin of the posterior process of the jugal present in NHMUK R3142 (MDE, 20 August 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=157 TAXON=16 TEXT='Based on Evans (1980: 212) (MDE, 20 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=157 TAXON=38 TEXT='This character is scored as unkown based on Nosotti (2007) (MDE, 2 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=157 TAXON=73 TEXT='The supratemporal of SAM-PK-6536 is considerably broader than the slit-like bone of Proterosuchus fergusi. Accordingly, it is scores as condition (0) (MDE, 27 August 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=157 TAXON=99 TEXT='However, the specimen that I identified as Prolacerta broomi in the GHG collection (431) seems to lack supratemporals and a supratemporal facet in both squamosals (MDE, 19 June 2012). Is this specimen actually Prolacerta broomi?';
TEXT CHARACTER=157 TAXON=104 TEXT='Both supratemporals are clearly present in SAM-PK-K10603 and SAM-PK-K140 (MDE, 19 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=159 TAXON=24 TEXT='Gottman-Quesada and Sander (2009: 142) (MDE, 10 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=159 TAXON=38 TEXT='In small individuals the parietals are not fused to each other, whereas the opposite occurs in large individuals (Nosotti 2007: 51). We have considered here only the adult condition (MDE, 11 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=160 TAXON=60 TEXT='The parietals do not extend over the interorbital region in TMM 31025-140 (Spielmann et al. 2008: fig. 19) (MDE, 4 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=160 TAXON=104 TEXT='Proterosuchus fergusi possesses intraspecific variation for this character, in large specimens (e.g. SAM-PK-K10603) the parietal does not extend over the interorbital region, but in smaller specimens (e.g. RC 59) the parietal considerably extends over the interorbital region. Probably it is related to an ontogenetic variation (MDE, 19 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=164 TAXON=9 TEXT='The dorsal surface of the parietals are too damaged to determine confidently the size and shape of the pineal foramen (MDE, 14 February 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=164 TAXON=15 TEXT='25.5% based on Fraser (1982: fig. 1c). Accordingly, the scoring of this character was changed from (1) to (0) (MDE, 11 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=164 TAXON=16 TEXT='Ratio=21.67% based on Evans (1980: fig. 9a) (MDE, 20 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=164 TAXON=24 TEXT='Gottman-Quesada and Sander (2009: 142) described that the presence of a pineal foramen seems to be a variable condition in Protorosaurus (MDE, 3 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=164 TAXON=38 TEXT='The size of the pineal foramen seems to range between 26.90% to 18.09% (Wild, 1973: fig. 1) (MDE, 20 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=164 TAXON=73 TEXT='Ratio=18.89% based on SAM-PK-6536 (Dilkes, 1998: fig. 5) (MDE, 27 August 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=164 TAXON=101 TEXT='Based on Tatarinov (1978: 508) (MDE, 2 April 2015).';
TEXT CHARACTER=164 TAXON=104 TEXT='In only one specimen of Proterosuchus fergusi I have seen a very small pineal foramen (BP/1/3993). In other well-preserved specimens the pineal foramen is definitely absent (e.g. RC 59, SAM-PK-K10603). So, this character seems to be polymorphic, as in Prolacerta broomi (MDE, 19 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=164 TAXON=141 TEXT='In well-preserved specimens of Erythrosuchus africanus (e.g. NM QR 1473) the pineal foramen is absent (MDE, 22 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=165 TAXON=1 TEXT='Borderline_--_depends_on_left_vs_right_parietal..._(DM)';
TEXT CHARACTER=165 TAXON=5 TEXT='Ratio_suture_anterior/posterior_to_foramen_in_Carroll_1981:_fig._9:_7.15/5.58_(ML)';
TEXT CHARACTER=165 TAXON=38 TEXT='In different specimens the pineal foramen is positioned at the frontal-parietal suture or it is completely enclosed by the parietals (Nosotti 2007: 51). As a result, this character was scored as polymorphic for Tanystropheus longobardicus (MDE, 2 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=165 TAXON=104 TEXT='Scoring based on BP/1/3993 (MDE, 19 June 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=170 TAXON=149 TEXT='Nesbitt et al. (2013: 11) (MDE, 25 September 2014).';
TEXT CHARACTER=171 TAXON=60 TEXT='The postparietal cannot be discerned in Trilophosaurus buettneri (Gregory 1945: 278) (MDE, 4 September 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=171 TAXON=73 TEXT='Dilkes (1998: character 29) scores Mesosuchus as lacking of a postparietal (MDE, 27 August 2012).';
TEXT CHARACTER=171 TAXON=99 TEXT='The postparietals are absent in Prolacerta broomi (Modesto and Sues, 2004). Accordingly, the scording of this character was changed from (1/2) to (2) (MDE, 11 August 2013).';
TEXT CHARACTER=177 TAXON=158 TEXT='angle = 123 (MDE, 23 June 2020)';
TEXT CHARACTER=177 TAXON=290 TEXT='ca. 135 grades (MDE, 06 November 2019)';
